C 0x6302 The low five bits times eight: the column
C 0x6309 The row, from 0xEC04
C 0x630E With row 0xF8 it sets 0x18, and otherwise 0xFF
C 0x6316 0xF8 or 0xFF depending on where it comes from
C 0x6318 Fifteen
C 0x631A 0xE1FF to zero
C 0x631B 0xE109: which script row it is on
L 0x6324 background_object_type   In stage 3 the type comes from another calculation; in the rest, bit 7 chooses between 1 and 2
C 0x6327 Stage 3 goes another way
C 0x632D Bit 7: one of the two types
C 0x6332 Two bits of C: one of four types
D 0x633A 0x6340 table_633A  Three words (0x6340, 0x6350, 0x6360) read by 0x61F2.
F 0x633A w2
D 0x6340 0x6370 formations  Forty-eight bytes the table above points to, and which p00:4B9F also asks for with `ld de,0x6340`.
F 0x6340 16
D 0x6370 0x64D4 trajectories  What 0x61F7 reads with `ld hl,0x6370`, in one run.
F 0x6370 16
D 0x64D4 0x64FA table_64D4  Thirty-eight bytes read by 0x626A.
F 0x64D4 8
D 0x64FA 0x65DC table_64FA  What 0x62DC reads with `ld hl,0x64FA`.
F 0x64FA 16
L 0x65DC run_ten_at_e500   The ten objects at 0xE500: adds their speed to them, checks whether they collide and switches off the ones that go off screen
C 0x65E0 Ten objects
C 0x65E8 Adds their speed to them, and returns whether they are still inside
C 0x65F1 And bank 2 checks whether they have collided with anything
C 0x65F6 Past Y 0xB0 or X 0xF0, they are gone
C 0x660B Thirty-two bytes: the next object
L 0x6613 enemy_shoots   Sets up a shot towards the ship: the speed comes from the difficulty, capped at 0x60
C 0x6613 With the screen stopped there is no shooting
C 0x661C The difficulty times two plus 0x50...
C 0x6622 ...capped at 0x60
C 0x6624 Capped at 0x60
C 0x6635 The ten slots at 0xE500
C 0x6640 Thirty-two bytes: the next one
L 0x6646 set_up_shot   Fills the shot's slot with its position and the two speeds that 0x6677 left in 0xEC12 and 0xEC14
C 0x6646 0xE112 to one: there is a new shot
C 0x6648 0xE112 to one: there is a new shot
C 0x664F The counters, to zero
C 0x6658 The vertical speed...
C 0x665F ...and the horizontal one
C 0x6668 The pattern and the colour
