C 0x6AA3 Three free slots in a row
C 0x6AA4 Compared with zero: free slot
C 0x6AA5 Thirty-two bytes: the next slot
C 0x6AB2 Go back to the first of the three
C 0x6AB7 And two more in the live count: it is three slots
L 0x6ABF search_other_table   Type 0x0E lives at 0xE460, eight slots counted backwards
C 0x6ABF Type 0x0E goes to the table at 0xE460
C 0x6AC4 Eight slots counting backwards
L 0x6AC7 find_free_slot   The first one with its first byte at zero
L 0x6ACE set_up_object   Fills the slot: type, counters to zero, the position, and the four bytes from the table at 0x6BA3
C 0x6ACE The position, which was parked in 0xEC19
C 0x6AD3 One more in the count of live objects
C 0x6AE1 Byte 27 to three
C 0x6AED The Y goes to byte 4...
C 0x6AF0 ...and the X to byte 6
C 0x6AF5 The table at 0x6BA3: four bytes per type
C 0x6AFB Times four
C 0x6B02 Three bytes of the type's record
C 0x6B09 With the adjustment set, byte 13 carries 8; type 0x0D, 6
C 0x6B0C Byte 13: eight, or six if it is type 0x0D
C 0x6B0D Type 0x0D carries six
C 0x6B21 The speed, which comes from the difficulty and the R register
