D 0x6B46 0x6B84 dispatcher_table_6B43  Thirty-one words stuck right after the `call 0x4067` at 0x6B43. Almost all the destinations fall in bank 3 (0xA000-0xBFFF).
F 0x6B46 w2
B 0x6B84 THE SPEED OF THE SHOTS: DIFFICULTY PLUS R REGISTER
B 0x6B84 The speed a shot comes out with is neither fixed nor truly random: it
B 0x6B84 takes from the table at 0x6B97 the value that belongs to the difficulty
B 0x6B84 (0xE111, twelve steps from 0x80 to 0x1C, that is, the harder the faster)
B 0x6B84 and ADDS to it whatever three bits of the Z80's R register say, the
B 0x6B84 memory refresh one. It is the third time this cartridge uses R as a
B 0x6B84 number generator: the other two are the background stars and the
B 0x6B84 shrapnel of the explosion, both in bank 0.
L 0x6B84 shot_speed   The speed step the difficulty says, plus zero to seven from the R register
C 0x6B85 0xE111 is the difficulty
C 0x6B90 The R register: three bits of unevenness
D 0x6B97 0x6BA3 speeds_by_difficulty  Twelve speed steps, one per difficulty level (0xE111), going downhill: 0x80, 0x70, 0x68, 0x60, 0x48, 0x40, 0x38, 0x30, 0x28, 0x24, 0x20 and 0x1C. The lower the number, the faster the shot goes. Read by 0x6B88, which also adds three bits of the R register to them.
F 0x6B97 12
D 0x6BA3 0x6C23 records_by_type  Four bytes per object type, which 0x6AF5 copies as they are to the freshly set-up slot: it is each enemy's starting record. Thirty-two types.
F 0x6BA3 4
